    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d352">

                <pb facs="0346" n="336" xml:id="pg336"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">835.796/141½</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Under Secretary of State</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Welles</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Assistant
                        Secretary of State</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Acheson</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-06-23">June 23, 1941</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Acheson</hi>: The Argentine Ambassador left with
                    me this morning a copy of an <hi rendition="#italic">aide-mémoire</hi> which he
                    left with the Department on May 21 last.<anchor n="29" xml:id="d352-f1"/> The
                    Argentine Navy is very anxious to have us grant the request comprised in this
                    memorandum. It is disturbed that we have not yet given any indication of a
                    favorable attitude.</p>
                <p>I shall appreciate it if you will have some one in your office follow this
                    through and see what the situation may be.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>S[<hi rendition="#small-caps">umner</hi>] W[<hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >elles</hi>]</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d352-f1" n="29" xml:id="d352-f1-content">
                <p><hi rendition="#italic">Supra</hi>.</p>
